// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 2 „Linn, teenused ja asjaajamine” (b1b2-006…010), stage B1+.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). One storyline a year after
// the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Jaan (kitchen head at Kase kool, plans a café) and Kadri need a bigger home than
// their three-room flat in Männi 8 — renting in Kristiine or buying an old flat in Nõmme (Vahtra 5) — and they deal with
// the bank, the city's e-services and officials, the housing association and the renovation. The goal, said on the first
// sheet: at the end the learner writes an official request to the district government and talks to the official (009
// Kasuta). Housing topic the B2 course lacked: renting vs buying, a home loan, the housing association, utility bills,
// a renovation and its permits.
// Grammar added here (B12H, METHODOLOGY_STANDARD §5 B2): total vs partial subject in existential clauses — Majas on lift /
// Majas ei ole lifti / Lähedal on kohvikuid; Külalised tulid / Külalisi tuli palju — noticed and practised in 006
// (Avasta table, Harjuta transformation, Kasuta letter), met again in 008 (defects: Keldris on vett, errorfix) and 009
// (Nõmmel on palju vanu puumaju, formtext). Kept from the module plan: locatives with movement (006), the conditional for
// polite requests (007), cause and effect seetõttu / mistõttu in a complaint (008), asking back and reacting to change
// (009). Module 1's daily-life words (kõigepealt, seejärel, seetõttu, kuigi, samas, plaan, eesmärk, kokkulepe…) return.
//   006 Kadri's post „rent or buy?”, Jaan calls the estate agent Evelin; the house rules, the flat ad, a route message;
//       the family decides (pro / contra cards) and Jaan writes Helgi how to find the flat.
//   007 the loan meeting with Allan at the bank, the bank's guide; Eneli's e-services talk at the library, the parking
//       permit guide; the city's phone line and the official Ingrid at the Nõmme district government desk.
//   008 the heating bill twice as high: Jaan's complaint and Urmas's answer, Kerli's voice message; the consumer advice,
//       the Männi 8 house chat (Karl, Leida); the general meeting and a formal complaint to Kodu Hooldus.
//   009 the renovation: three unexpected messages (the builder Rando, Ingrid, Eda of the Vahtra 5 association), the
//       district's letter on the milieu area; the builder's call, an article on Nõmme's old houses, the window debate;
//       street works all summer — the module's final task: an official request and a meeting with Ingrid.
// Final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md, 2026-10-29): 006 LUGE R→S (corner R3 = the flat ad cloze; main = S17
// argument cards rent vs buy), 007 RÄÄK L→S (corner W1 = the letter to the builders, W12; main = S10 at Ingrid's desk),
// 008 KIRJ L→W (corner S1 = S16 1-minute talk at the housing association meeting; main = W13 formal complaint), 009 PROJ
// R→W (corner S2 = S17 argument cards on the windows; main = the request to the district, W08 as a reply to the city's
// announcement). Every Kasuta has a pair task in the lesson and an S15 recording at home; two fluency tasks a lesson.
